"it tests the right thing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:21
msgid ""
"**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the "
"rules.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:23
msgid "When to Use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:25
msgid "**Always:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:26
msgid "New features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:27
msgid "Bug fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:28
msgid "Refactoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:29
msgid "Behavior changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:31
msgid "**Exceptions (ask the user first):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:32
msgid "Throwaway prototypes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:33
msgid "Generated code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:34
msgid "Configuration files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:36
msgid "Thinking \"skip TDD just this once\"? Stop. That's rationalization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:38
msgid "The Iron Law"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:44
msgid "Write code before the test? Delete it. Start over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:46
msgid "**No exceptions:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:47
msgid "Don't keep it as \"reference\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:48
msgid "Don't \"adapt\" it while writing tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:49
msgid "Don't look at it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:50
msgid "Delete means delete"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:52
msgid "Implement fresh from tests. Period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:54
msgid "Red-Green-Refactor Cycle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:56
msgid "RED — Write Failing Test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:58
msgid "Write one minimal test showing what should happen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:60
msgid "**Good test:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:76
msgid "Clear name, tests real behavior, one thing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:78
msgid "**Bad test:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:86
msgid "Vague name, tests mock not real code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:88
msgid "**Requirements:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:89
msgid "One behavior per test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:90
msgid "Clear descriptive name (\"and\" in name? Split it)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:91
msgid "Real code, not mocks (unless truly unavoidable)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:92
msgid "Name describes behavior, not implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:94
msgid "Verify RED — Watch It Fail"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:96
msgid "**MANDATORY. Never skip.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:103
#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:152
msgid "Confirm:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:104
msgid "Test fails (not errors from typos)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:105
msgid "Failure message is expected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:106
msgid "Fails because the feature is missing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:108
msgid ""
"**Test passes immediately?** You're testing existing behavior. Fix the "
"test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:110
msgid "**Test errors?** Fix the error, re-run until it fails correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:112
msgid "GREEN — Minimal Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:114
msgid "Write the simplest code to pass the test. Nothing more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:116
msgid "**Good:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:122
msgid "**Bad:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:130
msgid "Don't add features, refactor other code, or \"improve\" beyond the test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:132
msgid "**Cheating is OK in GREEN:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:133
msgid "Hardcode return values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:134
msgid "Copy-paste"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:135
msgid "Duplicate code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:136
msgid "Skip edge cases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:138
msgid "We'll fix it in REFACTOR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:140
msgid "Verify GREEN — Watch It Pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:142
msgid "**MANDATORY.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:153
msgid "Test passes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:154
msgid "Other tests still pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:155
msgid "Output pristine (no errors, warnings)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:157
msgid "**Test fails?** Fix the code, not the test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:159
msgid "**Other tests fail?** Fix regressions now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:161
msgid "REFACTOR — Clean Up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:163
msgid "After green only:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:164
msgid "Remove duplication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:165
msgid "Improve names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:166
msgid "Extract helpers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:167
msgid "Simplify expressions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:169
msgid "Keep tests green throughout. Don't add behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:171
msgid "**If tests fail during refactor:** Undo immediately. Take smaller steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:173
msgid "Repeat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:175
msgid "Next failing test for next behavior. One cycle at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:177
msgid "Why Order Matters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:179
msgid "**\"I'll write tests after to verify it works\"**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:181
msgid ""
"Tests written after code pass immediately. Passing immediately proves "
"nothing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:182
msgid "Might test the wrong thing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:183
msgid "Might test implementation, not behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:184
msgid "Might miss edge cases you forgot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:185
msgid "You never saw it catch the bug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:187
msgid ""
"Test-first forces you to see the test fail, proving it actually tests "
"something."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:189
msgid "**\"I already manually tested all the edge cases\"**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:191
msgid "Manual testing is ad-hoc. You think you tested everything but:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:192
msgid "No record of what you tested"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:193
msgid "Can't re-run when code changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:194
msgid "Easy to forget cases under pressure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:195
msgid "\"It worked when I tried it\" ≠ comprehensive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:197
msgid "Automated tests are systematic. They run the same way every time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:199
msgid "**\"Deleting X hours of work is wasteful\"**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:201
msgid "Sunk cost fallacy. The time is already gone. Your choice now:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:202
msgid "Delete and rewrite with TDD (high confidence)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:203
msgid "Keep it and add tests after (low confidence, likely bugs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:205
msgid "The \"waste\" is keeping code you can't trust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:207
msgid "**\"TDD is dogmatic, being pragmatic means adapting\"**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:209
msgid "TDD IS pragmatic:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:210
msgid "Finds bugs before commit (faster than debugging after)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:211
msgid "Prevents regressions (tests catch breaks immediately)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:212
msgid "Documents behavior (tests show how to use code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:213
msgid "Enables refactoring (change freely, tests catch breaks)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:215
msgid "\"Pragmatic\" shortcuts = debugging in production = slower."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:217
msgid "**\"Tests after achieve the same goals — it's spirit not ritual\"**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:219
msgid ""
"No. Tests-after answer \"What does this do?\" Tests-first answer \"What "
"should this do?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:221
msgid ""
"Tests-after are biased by your implementation. You test what you built, "
"not what's required. Tests-first force edge case discovery before "
"implementing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:223
msgid "Common Rationalizations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "Excuse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "Reality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"Too simple to test\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "Simple code breaks. Test takes 30 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"I'll test after\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "Tests passing immediately prove nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"Tests after achieve same goals\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this "
"do?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"Already manually tested\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "Ad-hoc ≠ systematic. No record, can't re-run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"Deleting X hours is wasteful\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "Sunk cost fallacy. Keeping unverified code is technical debt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"Keep as reference, write tests first\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "You'll adapt it. That's testing after. Delete means delete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"Need to explore first\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "Fine. Throw away exploration, start with TDD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"Test hard = design unclear\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "Listen to the test. Hard to test = hard to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"TDD will slow me down\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "TDD faster than debugging. Pragmatic = test-first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"Manual test faster\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "Manual doesn't prove edge cases. You'll re-test every change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "\"Existing code has no tests\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md
msgid "You're improving it. Add tests for the code you touch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:239
msgid "Red Flags — STOP and Start Over"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:241
msgid ""
"If you catch yourself doing any of these, delete the code and restart "
"with TDD:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:243
msgid "Code before test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:244
msgid "Test after implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:245
msgid "Test passes immediately on first run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:246
msgid "Can't explain why test failed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:247
msgid "Tests added \"later\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:248
msgid "Rationalizing \"just this once\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:249
msgid "\"I already manually tested it\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:250
msgid "\"Tests after achieve the same purpose\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:251
msgid "\"Keep as reference\" or \"adapt existing code\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:252
msgid "\"Already spent X hours, deleting is wasteful\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:253
msgid "\"TDD is dogmatic, I'm being pragmatic\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:254
msgid "\"This is different because...\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:256
msgid "**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:258
msgid "Verification Checklist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:260
msgid "Before marking work complete:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:262
msgid "[ ] Every new function/method has a test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:263
msgid "[ ] Watched each test fail before implementing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:264
msgid "[ ] Each test failed for expected reason (feature missing, not typo)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:265
msgid "[ ] Wrote minimal code to pass each test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:266
msgid "[ ] All tests pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:267
msgid "[ ] Output pristine (no errors, warnings)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:268
msgid "[ ] Tests use real code (mocks only if unavoidable)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:269
msgid "[ ] Edge cases and errors covered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/test-driven-development_SKILL.md:271
msgid "Can't check all boxes? You skipped TDD. Start over."
msgstr ""

